  "email": "priya.nair@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Identify ticket sender, location, and devices for office-wide outage report"
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-LT-0103",
  "reason": "Confirm whether the sender's laptop has lost connectivity as part of the office outage"
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-PR-FL2",
  "reason": "Check whether another device on the office network (floor printer) is also offline, to gauge the outage scope"
}

{
  "summary": "P1: Office-wide internet outage reported by Priya Nair (IT Manager, user_id 3, America/New_York). She says the whole office lost internet and nobody on the floor can work. Checks: account active, no issues. Her laptop BL-LT-0103 shows online, last check-in 2026-10-09T14:16:18Z (she may be on a hotspot or another path, or the check-in came just before the outage; not confirmed). Floor printer BL-PR-FL2 is offline, last check-in 2026-10-09T09:22:18Z. That is about 5 hours earlier, so it may be unrelated or may point to an earlier fault on the floor network. Tier 1 has no tools to check the office WAN/ISP link, firewall, core switches, or Wi-Fi controllers. Still needed: check the site uplink/ISP circuit, firewall/router, core switch, DHCP/DNS; contact the ISP if the circuit is down; send status updates to the affected staff. Per KB-014, an office network outage affecting several people means escalation, and this ticket is P1.",
  "reason": "P1 office-wide network outage; KB-014 escalation criteria met; beyond Tier 1 tools"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Priya, thanks for reporting this. Because the whole floor is down, I've sent it to our Tier 2 network team as a top-priority outage. They'll check the office internet line, the firewall and the core network equipment, and they'll contact the internet provider if the line itself is down. Meanwhile, anyone who has to work urgently can use a phone hotspot. Please don't restart any shared network equipment unless the network team asks you to. If you notice anything about how it started, like when it began, alarm lights on network equipment, a power blip, or whether wired and Wi-Fi are both down, reply here and we'll pass it straight to the network team.",
  "internal_note": "P1 office-wide internet outage reported by Priya Nair (IT Manager, user_id 3). Her account is active with no issues. Her laptop BL-LT-0103 shows online, last check-in 2026-10-09 14:16Z. She may be on another connection; not confirmed. Floor printer BL-PR-FL2 is offline, last check-in 09:22Z. That is about 5 hours before the report, so it may be unrelated or may point to an earlier fault on the floor network. Tier 1 can't see the WAN/ISP link, firewall, switches or Wi-Fi controllers. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation id 1) under KB-014's escalation rule and the P1 priority. Tier 2 needs to check the uplink/ISP circuit, firewall, core switch and DHCP/DNS, then send status updates to the staff affected.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-014"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
